free
Usage: free [-bkmgh]

Show how much memory is used and how much is free.

	-b	bytes
	-k	kilobytes (the default)
	-m	megabytes
	-g	gigabytes
	-h	human readable -- pick the unit per value

On xos every writable byte is tmpfs, which is RAM. Files you create
under /tmp or your home therefore show up as used memory, and are gone
at reboot.

See also: df, du, top, ps
